D={
381155:('rainbow.html','PARK_NO_FULL_EXACT_MECHANISM','Source abstract and initial introduction only; exact corpus statement read.','Gallai decomposition reduces to recursively two-colored quotient graphs, but no proof of the exact Ramsey product threshold is supplied. The r,t universal claim is not established by its t=3 check or the source\'s two-color-subset asymptotic theorem. No flagship investment without a full mechanism.'),
326412:('weak.html','HOLD_MINOR_FAMILY_GAP','Introductory family/weak-orientation definitions; source family construction and all-minor proof not read.','A proof must supply weak orientations for every one-element deletion and contraction uniformly in n and use minor closure to cover every proper minor. Small checked n<=2 do not do this; the exact MI_n construction is a material unread input. No finite counterexample proposed.'),
326795:('trees.html','HOLD_INFINITE_CLASSIFICATION_AND_FIGURE','Source introduction and reconstruction/class-reconstruction definitions; actual T_k figure not inspected.','The endpoint concerns infinite classes, not an isolated exceptional tree. Need either a new infinite family with ern=3 and nonmembership in all three listed families, or full exclusion of every other infinite family. Neither an edge-card reconstruction mechanism nor an explicit infinite counterfamily is proved.'),
330886:('embedding.html','EXCLUDE_DOMAIN_CORRECTION_ONLY','Source Section 2 half-cube/truncated metric definitions and Section 5 Conjecture 1; one arXiv version, Wiley journal body unavailable under inherited access constraint.','One-letter graphs are complete and have an explicit half-cube embedding, but source 2-truncated definition requires diameter>=2. Correcting omitted n/diameter restrictions is zero credit. Beyond the endpoint, no parameter-uniform local obstruction; see ORDINARY.md.'),
323970:('snarks.html','EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_SOURCE_REFUTATION','Source Theorem 1.1, Conjecture 1.4, definitions and early gluing/PCDC proof passages. Entire construction/figures not audited.','Theorem 1.1 at n=1 has order 34, cyclic edge connectivity 5 and a disjoint two-circuit permutation factor not extendible to a CDC; it is not Petersen. This is the source\'s own full-scope counterexample family, not new credit.'),
330940:('tanglegram.html','EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_COMPANION_PROOF','Original literal statement plus companion Corollary 4 and proof excerpt, total variation proof tail and tree moments. Original entire body not read.','Konvalinka–Wagner 1512.01168v2 Corollary 4 proves precisely E(cherries)~n/4. Bounded normalized counts transfer expectations under total variation convergence. Full bridge and chronology in ORDINARY.md. No new credit.'),
325964:('theta.html','HOLD_THETA_CERTIFICATE_MISSING','Source introductory Fourier/Cayley setup excerpts; full final theta conjecture proof search incomplete.','Fixing a nonzero vector supplies the lower bound. An independence bound alone does not force theta equal to alpha: need a feasible dual theta/character certificate attaining the same product for every n,q. None derived. Existing finite numerical checks are not exact certificates or universal proof.'),
329797:('diagram.html','HOLD_SOURCE_STATUS_CONFLICT','Source introduction, positroid definition/Theorem 3.7 proof excerpts; diagram-matroid conjecture and all dependencies not fully read.','The record simultaneously says conjectural/checked S7 and references solved. Neither metadata label resolves this. Need actual diagram-matroid definition and a rank-generating bijection preserving subset size/rank for all permutations, or a genuine explicit mismatch. Existing positroid decomposition alone is not that bijection.'),
330457:('matching.html','PARK_UNIFORM_ALGORITHM_GAP','Actual source Theorem 1.1 and Conjecture 1; source describes it as challenging, not refuted.','A finite forbidden graph M is input to a uniform complexity classification, not a finite test instance that refutes it. The long-claw algorithm covers one subclass, not every subdivided claw or disjoint union. The source provides no refutation despite parser status. No complete algorithm/hardness counterfamily obtained.'),
338717:('enumeration.html','PARK_UNLABELLED_COUNTING_GAP','Source Section 1.3, actual Conjecture 1.5 and labelled recurrence context read.','Labelled polynomial recurrences cannot simply be divided by n!: automorphism groups vary. Burnside requires fixed-point counts for all cycle types and an efficient aggregation; no polynomial uniform-in-n procedure for each fixed k derived. k=1,2 known special cases are zero-credit helpers.'),
354781:('squares.html','PARK_UNIFORM_ANALYTIC_GAP','Source abstract, introductory definitions and known-threshold context; later exact target passage not fully surfaced.','Orthogonality expands the fourth moment into weighted equal-sum-of-two-squares collisions. Bounding each individual multiplicity uniformly over all intervals at every gamma<1 remains unproved. The gamma<golden-ratio-inverse source improvement and Sidon range are incomplete for the full quantifier. No finite computation can prove this analytic uniformity.'),
354874:('convex.html','HOLD_VERSION_AND_GEOMETRY_SCOPE','Latest v3 introduction and open-problem inventory; the recorded almost-holey conjecture was not located there.','Malformed point-set notation in the corpus is preserved, not silently repaired. Need older source passage and hypotheses (including family distinctness/position conventions) before constructing an exact geometric object. Pairwise intersections do not alone bound m; triple intersections and convex hull/source correspondence are essential. No in-scope object or full proof supplied.'),
354926:('flip.html','PARK_GRAPHON_LOWER_BOUND_GAP','Acquired complete source; introductory excerpts were surfaced with aggregate truncation, no complete lower-time definition/proof review.','A proof needs the exact lower convergence time over graphons and all single-destination convergent rules, not just constant graphons or a linearization at equilibrium. No comparison principle controlling every such rule with the sharp factor 2(k)_2 is proved. Stored bytes are not source-definition clearance.'),
354961:('vandermonde.html','EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_SOURCE_PROOF','Actual matrix definition, restatement 4.9, and full local proof Section 4.3 read. Generic-MDS supporting dependencies not independently reconstructed.','Exact recorded criterion is proved in its cited source. Kernel differences, glued word, complement-support syndromes and generic intersection dimension yield contradiction. Full bridge in ORDINARY.md. Empty-subset wording also needs the usual nonempty interpretation; that correction earns zero credit.'),
354963:('chromatic.html','PARK_FULL_TREE_DISTINGUISHING_GAP','Acquired complete primary HTML; general conjectural introductory excerpts surfaced, no full finite-specialization proof review.','A single finite principal specialization is a univariate polynomial and need not recover an arbitrary symmetric function. No injectivity theorem on all tree chromatic symmetric functions at the stated vertex/color cutoff is provided. The isomorphic=>equal direction is a routine invariant helper; neither full converse nor a specific nonisomorphic equal-specialization pair obtained.'),
354975:('gluing.html','HOLD_TOPOLOGICAL_DEFINITIONS_AND_ENDPOINT','Acquired source; some graph embedding classification/proof excerpts surfaced with aggregate truncation, not the exact gluing conjecture proof.','IPPI3L and separating planar vertex must be matched to projective-plane link definitions. A shared-vertex decomposition does not alone show a forced three-link in every embedding. Need a full homological case argument with the nonouter and closed-nonseparating hypotheses; none established.'),
355013:('c2.html','PARK_ALL_PRIMES_PREMISE_GAP','Actual Kirchhoff/c2 definitions and primitive graph setup; source introductory weaker-result context read.','The source\'s relation modulo p at prime powers is weaker than an identity modulo p^s. A finite graph-pair counterexample would still require proving equality at EVERY prime in the antecedent. A discrepancy at one prime-power alone is insufficient. No all-primes mechanism, exact graph pair, or full lift theorem found.'),
355016:('derived.html','HOLD_SUSTAINED_ELIMINATION_GAP','Source Definitions 4.1–4.3, Remark 4.4, high-rank restricted proof, Lemma 8.1 and conjecture; earlier-version weak-order sections; journal Conjecture 43 and definitions, companion rank-bound introduction.','Three routes sustained: nullity/iteration induction, minimal-circuit refinement, and maximal-matroid rank bounds. All stop at representation-specific unmarked dependencies or unmet submodularity/identification hypotheses. Explicit ordinary diagnostic in ORDINARY.md is not a realized matroid counterexample.'),
355426:('resistance.html','HOLD_SUSTAINED_INDEX_RECURRENCE_VALUATION_GAPS','Actual transform/grid/local-edge definitions and proof passages; uniform-center theorem proof; Section 7 and Conjecture 8.1, older v1 analogous passages; companion introduction. Journal only search-visible excerpts.','Uniform-boundary equation has an auxiliary Bs, and the literal row s is outside the stated uniform-center starting row s+d. Full local formulas introduce other diagonals; no semantically correct closed recurrence and no reduced-numerator valuation invariant. Three route stages in ORDINARY.md; source monotonicity itself is known.'),
355433:('bidding.html','HOLD_SUSTAINED_CONTEXTUAL_INTERPOLATION_GAP','Latest definitions, auction, Conjecture 68 and Theorems 18–28 proof passages; earlier v1 and companion outcome-monotonicity proof excerpts. Journal institutional metadata only, body unread.','Reverse implication is strict-order transitivity. Forward birthday induction gives number options but not interpolation of H. Inverse translation still needs a 0-bid strategy for all contexts/partitions; standalone outcomes and marker monotonicity do not establish it. No contextual witness or general strategy proved; see ORDINARY.md.')
}
